# Local drafts and working files — not for publication.
# Article prose stays off GitHub to avoid duplicate-content penalties on Medium.
# Only README.md is published from an article folder; every other top-level .md
# in one (article.md, submitted.md, corrected.md, …) is a working draft.
# Note: code-samples/*.md sit two levels deep and are unaffected by this.
*/*.md
!*/README.md

# Variant images, scratch renders, and other working artifacts.
*/archives/

# An article's figures live in support-files/ to keep the article folder itself
# down to what a reader wants: README, header, and the images the piece embeds.
# support-files/ is published — diagram source belongs there. Anything that is
# only useful on this machine (raw .png renders, render scripts, rejected
# variants, scratch) goes one level down into local/ and never ships.
*/support-files/local/

# Articles with no companion code — Medium-only, kept locally for reference.
hitl-article/

# Internal session handoff notes — never published.
*/HANDOFF.md

# Requirements / source-material trees behind a series — planning input, not deliverables.
ai-infra/requirements/

# Local Claude Code config / skills — not part of the repo.
.claude/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Working rules for my own tooling — local only, not published.
/CLAUDE.md
